  "query_preview": "..\nSynopsis:\nAn upper ridge will build over the northern plains through Friday\nas a cut-off low is positioned off the Pacific NW coast. SW flow\nover the area develops into Saturday will allow for clouds to\nincrease through Saturday. The upper low then becomes an upper\ntrough then moves inland Saturday night and Sunday. This will help\nspread an area of rain northeast into the CWA Sunday night.\n\nThis rain is expected to move out Monday as an upper ridge moves\nin from the west.\n\nTemperatures through Friday are expected to be slightly below\nnormal then slightly above normal this weekend into early next\nweek. \n\nConditions for the Trick or Treaters late Saturday should be dry\nwith little wind.\n\nDon't forget to set your clocks back an hour Saturday night.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nNo deviations from the NBM.\n\nAlthough low clouds and patchy fog are possible this morning that\nthe NBM hasn't handled 100 percent, so some tweaks in the forecast\nare possible later this morning. TFJ",
